                "problem": "Here the real numbers satisfy the algebraic axioms of §4: (1) $+$ and $\\cdot$ are associative, (2) commutative, (3) there are distinct elements $0$ and $1$ with $x + 0 = x$ and $x \\cdot 1 = x$, (4) each $x$ has an additive inverse $-x$, and each $x \\neq 0$ a multiplicative inverse $1/x$, (5) $x \\cdot (y + z) = x \\cdot y + x \\cdot z$. One defines $x - y = x + (-y)$ and $x / y = x \\cdot (1/y)$. Prove the following \"laws of algebra\" for $\\mathbb{R}$, using only axioms (1)-(5) and the results proved in this section:\n    <ol class=\"math-list-alpha my-4\"><li class=\"my-4\">If $x + y = x$, then $y = 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$0 \\cdot x = 0$. [Hint: Compute $(x + 0) \\cdot x$.]</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$-0 = 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$-(-x) = x$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$x(-y) = -(xy) = (-x)y$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(-1)x = -x$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$x(y - z) = xy - xz$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$-(x + y) = -x - y$; $-(x - y) = -x + y$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">If $x \\neq 0$ and $x \\cdot y = x$, then $y = 1$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$x / x = 1$ if $x \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$x / 1 = x$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$x \\neq 0$ and $y \\neq 0 \\Rightarrow xy \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(1/y)(1/z) = 1/(yz)$ if $y, z \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(x/y)(w/z) = (xw)/(yz)$ if $y, z \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(x/y) + (w/z) = (xz + wy)/(yz)$ if $y, z \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$x \\neq 0 \\Rightarrow 1/x \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$1/(w/z) = z/w$ if $w, z \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(x/y)/(w/z) = (xz)/(yw)$ if $y, w, z \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(ax)/y = a(x/y)$ if $y \\neq 0$.</li>\n<li class=\"my-4\">$(-x)/y = x/(-y) = -(x/y)$ if $y \\neq 0$.</li></ol>"
